      "hints": [
        "For wires of the same metal, number density and carrier charge are the same in I = Anvq.",
        "Use the area ratio from part (ii)(1) to eliminate the area factor from the drift-speed ratio."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For each wire, I = Anvq. The same metal gives equal n and q for X and Y.",
        "Therefore I_X / I_Y = (A_X v_X) / (A_Y v_Y).",
        "Rearranging gives v_X / v_Y = (I_X / I_Y)(A_Y / A_X).",
        "Using I_X / I_Y = 0.60 / 1.8 and A_X / A_Y = 0.25 gives v_X / v_Y = (0.60 / 1.8)(1 / 0.25) = 1.3.",
        "The average drift-speed ratio X / Y is 1.3."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "deterministic_checks": [],
        "full_marks_if_all_deterministic_checks_pass": false,
        "ai_rubric": [
          {
